y to sustain and maintain its market share |\n\nPrice Increase\n\n---\n\n#### GIC Re \u2013 Strategic Approach and Way Forward (2/2)\n\n| Adoption of Modelling Capabilities | Phased adoption of modelling capabilities to ensure better exposure management and deriving value extraction from it |\n| --- | --- |\n| Focus on Underwriting Profitability | Continued Focus on underwriting profitability through: \u2013 Class-specific evaluation and weeding out the contracts with inadequate pricing \u2013 Incentivization based on individual company / contract performance |\n| Catastrophe Reserves for Climate Change | GIC Re has started building catastrophe reserves for climate change, which will help to better manage volatility in future |\n| Focus on maintaining and improving its Credit Rating | The company has a credit rating of A- Excellent from AM Best. We will Strive to improve the rating by continued focus on balance sheet strength, operating performance, market position and enterprise risk management |\n| Healthy capitalization | Significant Net Worth will now fuel Growth and Resilience. |\n| Focus on improving Net Incurred Claims and Commission ratio | GIC Re is focused on improving net incurred claims ratio by working towards reducing the attritional losses and commission ratios are expected to remain stable |\n\n---\n\n#### Sustainability at the Core: Leading with Green Practices\n\n##### Responsible consumption\n\n\u25b6 Digitalization of operations to reduce use of \npaper \u2013 workflow management\n\n\u25b6 Undertaking efforts towards \ndecarbonization \u2013 efforts to migrate \noperations to cloud native\n\n\u25b6 Board approved policies\n\n**Environment friendly business practices**\n\n## Environment friendly business Responsible consumption\n\n**practices**\n\n\u25b6 Preference for providing capacities that \naid transition towards low carbon \neconomy\n\n# Real Estate\n\n##### Protecting the environment\n\n\u25b6 Adopting green measures for \ncommunication\n\n\u25b6 Consideration of the environment and \nclimate change in investment decisions\n\n\u25b6 Investments made in green bonds\n\n---\n\n#### Championing Social Responsibility\n\n##### Shri Peetambara Shiksha Samiti FY2025-26\n\nIndependent Trusteeship of the University of Delhi\n\nD.E.C. No.\nInstitution of Medical Sciences, Delhi\n\nRegistration and Registration Number:\nINFSCN \n\n\u0938\u094d\u0925\u093e\u0928\u0940\u092f \u092c\u0928\u094d\u0926\u0930 \u0938\u0902\u0938\u094d\u0915\u0943\u0924\u093f HOSPITAL\n\n\u25b6 GIC Re collaborated with Shri Peetambara\nShiksha Samiti for upgradation of a 100-Bed\nHospital into a State-Of-The Art Multispecialty\nwith Blood Bank Facility and Community\nMobilization and outreach programmes in\nSitapur, Uttar Pradesh, India.\n\n\u25b6 The project intends strengthen rural healthcare\ninfrastructure and improve\noutcomes in Sitapur and nearby areas.\n\ncommunity health\n\n\u25b6 Thrust area \u2013 Healthcare.\n\n##### National Sports Development Fund (NSDF) - FY2025-26\n\nYOU CAN BE ANY WAY YOU LIKE TO BE\n\n\u25b6\n\nGIC Re collaborated with Sports Authority of India (NSDF)\ntowards Infrastructure enhancement (Fully Equipped Gym for\nPara Athletes, Jogging Track) at Jawahar Lal Nehru stadium,\nNew Delhi for World para Athletics Championship New Delhi\n2025\n\n\u25b6\n\nThrust area \u2013 Infrastructure Development & Government\nFunds\n\n##### Artificial Limbs Manufacturing Corporation of India (ALIMCO)\n\nGeneral Insurance Corporation of India GIC Re\nKantamal, Odisha, India\nMq32+wdf, Kantamal, Odisha 762017, India\nLat 20.85470\" Long 83.75082\"\nSaturday, 09/11/2025 11:38 AM\nGPS Map Capture\n\nJamuaira, Odisha, India\nRohitam, Black Office Acl, Jamuaira, Odisha 762014\nIndia\nLat 20.849068 Long 84.357473\nFloor: 31/10/2025 11:27 AM GMT\n\n\u25b6 GIC Re has collaborated with Artificial Limbs Manufacturing\nCorporation of India for contribution of CSR funds for providing\nfree daily assistive devices to senior citizens.\n\